A||||1||Coop88||Upper control arm fun for 88s||||1||
Z||000000||Coop88||06-01-2001||06:35 AM||||Went to take my formula in for an alignment the other day, and they told me that they couldn't align it because the control arm shafts wouldn't stay put. I replaced the originals with the ones from the fierostore. The originals have slots cut in the bottom of them so they can grip the frame. The replacements do not. The guy at the alignment shop said I need these slots cut into my shafts. Is there a way I can do it? Or am I at the mercy of the machine shop? <P>He also told me that the bolts would have to go in from the bottom. His reason was that the nuts kept turning with the bolts. I guess he can't fit a 18mm wrench in there with the tire in place. After looking at my front end, I found that there's no way the bolts are gonna go in through the bottom. So I'm gonna try to replace the paddle bolt assembly with some lock nuts welded into a 3/16" thick piece of steel. Has anyone ever tried/done this? Any tips or suggestions? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||06-01-2001||01:47 PM||||I just took the stock paddle nut assembly and had the nuts welded in place. No need to make anything new (except a special wrench to get in there and hold the nuts)||||reg||1
